<h2>What buyers still want to know</h2>
</div>
<div>
<div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Do I really need a burr grinder?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Yes, if you care about better coffee. Burr grinders create more consistent grounds than blade grinders, which helps extraction and makes coffee less muddy or uneven.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Is the Breville Smart Grinder Pro only for espresso?</summary><p class="faq-answer">No. It covers a broad range from espresso to drip, pour-over, French press, and cold brew, which is why it works well as a mainstream one-grinder decision.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>Is the Fellow Ode Gen 2 good for espresso?</summary><p class="faq-answer">No. The Fellow Ode Gen 2 is a strong premium grinder for brewed coffee, but it is not the right choice if espresso is part of the plan.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>How much grind adjustment do most people need?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Most people need enough range to dial in their main brew method without frustration. Very fine micro-adjustment matters more for espresso than for drip or French press.</p></details><details class="faq-item" open=""><summary>What matters more: burr quality or motor power?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Burr design, alignment, consistency, and adjustment usually matter more than raw motor claims. A strong motor does not guarantee good grind quality.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Is a grinder more important than the coffee maker?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Often, yes. A better grinder can improve almost every brew method because grind consistency affects extraction directly.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How often should a burr grinder be cleaned?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Light cleaning every few weeks is reasonable for regular use, with deeper cleaning less often depending on oily beans and how much coffee you grind.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Should I buy a grinder before upgrading my brewer?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Usually yes. If you are still using pre-ground coffee or a blade grinder, the grinder upgrade often delivers the bigger improvement.</p></details>
</div>
